1	# 02 · Draft order: staff can delete a draft they no longer need
2	
3	**Type:** Test coverage · **Area:** Orders / Drafts · **Priority:** Low
4	
5	## Context
6	
7	Drafts pile up: a customer abandons a phone order, or staff start one in the wrong channel.
8	Staff delete a draft from the draft page's menu, after a confirmation. We have no e2e coverage
9	of this; if deletion silently failed, the drafts list would keep filling with orders nobody can
10	get rid of.
11	
12	## What to cover
13	
14	1. Start a draft order in the USD channel.
15	2. Delete it from the draft's menu and confirm.
16	3. The draft is gone.
17	
18	## Acceptance criteria
19	
20	- [ ] After confirming, staff are taken back to the drafts list.
21	- [ ] Opening the deleted draft's address again shows the "page was not found" screen, not the
22	      draft.
23	
24	## Notes
25	
26	- Use the existing draft-order page object to start the draft.
27	- No new test infrastructure needed.
